  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "The current best is config_029 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 accuracy. The evidence strongly supports this architecture: scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 (~7% gain), imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, transformer > avgpool (~2% gain), and weighted > concat (small but consistent). The one remaining untested variant of this top architecture is config_007, which swaps fusion from weighted to concat while keeping transformer aggregation. This directly tests whether the fusion choice still matters under transformer aggregation (where the two modality representations are already being mixed by attention). If concat performs comparably, it confirms config_029 is near-optimal and we can lock in the best config with 2 experiments remaining for potential fine-tuning. If concat unexpectedly outperforms, we gain a new best. Expected cost is similar to config_029 (~3.5–4 GPU hours), keeping total well within budget and leaving room for 2 more experiments."
}

